Z||000000||MooCow||04-07-2000||02:15 PM||||I found yet another Fiero by me.  They now just seem to be popping up everyway.<BR>Well this Fiero I beleive as I drove by it said 1984 and wat a stick and had 99,000 miles on it and was asking $2,500 for it.  That price seems really high.  It was all red with some grayish color ground effects on it.  I'm going to go look at again and stop when the weather quites raining here.  What would you pay or offer for this?????<BR>                           Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||04-07-2000||02:23 PM||||If the car has the "aero" nose, notchback, and greyish highlights on the bottom edge it could be an 85 GT. 85 thru 87 GT's had grey on the bottom edge. Of course in 88 the aeromolding was the same color as the body. 86 thru 88 GT was the fastback body style. If the car in question is an 85 GT with a V-6 4spd and in excellent condition it could be worth $2500.00 But you will need to check out the car very well. If it's an 84 it has a 4cyl and a 4spd. The ground effects were probably painted or added by the previous owner. An 84 in excellent condition is worth about $1200 to $1600. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||04-08-2000||09:07 AM||||If it's an '84 <B>Indy</B>, then it's worth a little more depending on the condition.||||reg||1
